.TH XD\-KEYS 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-keys \- Passwords and Keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-keys
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-keys
manages stored passwords, SSH keys and PGP keys, as GNOME's Seahorse does,
in a Control Panel applet (User Accounts).
User Accounts' \(lqManage my network passwords\(rq opens it, as it opened
Stored User Names and Passwords in Windows XP.
Changes take effect at once.
.TP
.B Passwords
The keyrings of the Secret Service (GNOME Keyring, KeePassXC and others),
through libsecret: lock and unlock a keyring (the service asks for its
password); add, remove and rename passwords; show a password
(\(lqShow password\(rq), copy it and change it.
Properties also shows when it was stored and changed, and the attributes
programs look it up by.
.TP
.B SSH Keys
The key pairs in
.IR ~/.ssh ,
with their fingerprints and comments
.RB ( ssh\-keygen (1)
.BR \-l ):
make a new one (Ed25519 by default, or RSA or ECDSA), change its
passphrase, copy the public key to the clipboard, and delete it (to the
Recycle Bin).
Which keys
.BR ssh\-agent (1)
holds, and adding keys to it or removing them
.RB ( ssh\-add (1)).
.TP
.B PGP Keys
GnuPG's keyring, through gpgme: public keys and key pairs with their user
IDs, key IDs, fingerprints, expiry dates and trust; make a key pair
(Ed25519 and Curve25519), import keys from a file, export a public key
(armoured), delete a key, and change a key pair's expiry date.
.PP
Passphrases are asked for in its own dialogs.
For SSH keys,
.B xd\-keys
is the askpass program of the
.B ssh\-keygen
and
.B ssh\-add
it runs, and hands them the passphrases on a pipe; for PGP keys,
gpg\-agent asks it through loopback pinentry.
Passphrases never appear on a command line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on the
.IR n th
tab, from 0 (Passwords).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SSH_AUTH_SOCK
The SSH agent to list and load keys into.
.TP
.B GNUPGHOME
The GnuPG keyring, instead of
.IR ~/.gnupg .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-users (1),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1),
.BR ssh\-add (1),
.BR gpg (1),
.BR secret\-tool (1)
